# Keep agent docs and comments current

These materials exist so the **next** AI agent can understand the goal, the
structure, why decisions were made, and how to work here without rediscovering
them.

## Sources of truth

| Layer | Path |
| --- | --- |
| Agent handbook (start here) | `docs/agents/README.md` and numbered sections |
| Architecture / trust | `docs/architecture.md` |
| UI contract | `docs/ui/design-record.md` |
| Validation journeys | `docs/agent-paths.md` |
| File-level why/gotchas | library and class dartdoc / JSDoc in code |

## When you change code

In the **same** change (same PR), update docs and comments if you did any of:

1. Changed product behavior, routing, unlock rules, or kill switches.
2. Added/removed/renamed a reusable widget, provider, callable, or content
   renderer.
3. Encoded or reversed a user preference (teach-by-doing, one table, separate
   course/Live stats, fixed action buckets, lesson frame, etc.).
4. Moved responsibility between client and server.
5. Added an agent workflow, tool, or gotcha others will hit.

### What to update

- Touch the matching `docs/agents/0N-*.md` section(s). Add a new section file
  and link it from `docs/agents/README.md` when a whole subsystem appears.
- Update deep docs (`architecture.md`, `design-record.md`, `agent-paths.md`,
  `coaching-quality.md`) when their contracts actually change — do not
  duplicate them into the handbook.
- Refresh library/file comments: purpose, preference, and "do not undo"
  gotchas. Prefer short why-comments over narrating every line.
- If you add a preferred reusable component, add a row to
  `docs/agents/07-reusable-components.md`.

### What not to do

- Leave stale handbook claims that contradict the code you just shipped.
- Add noisy comments that only restate the next line of code.
- Put secrets, API keys, or private grading keys into docs or comments.
- Skip handbook updates because "the PR description explains it" — PR text
  is not durable context for the next agent.

## Quick check before merge

Ask: "If I were a new agent with only `docs/agents/` and the file headers,
would I know what changed and why?" If no, update them before you open the PR.
